# `CLASS-CHANNEL-REACH`: the class-channel check reaches this genre's collections.
# Until 0.4 it ran over `doc.edges` alone, and a `message` is NOT an
# edge (`SEQUENCE-ORDER-MODEL`: it has its own collection, because it has a position in time),
# so `class k "K" fill=#eee` plus `message c -> s "m" class=k` was accepted,
# painted nothing of the fill, and put the class in the derived legend.
#
# All three interior-less members of this genre are pinned — `message`,
# `fragment` and `operand` — because they reached the model by three
# different parse paths and one loop per collection is what closed them.
figdown 0.4 sequence
title "Class channels under sequence"
class ghost "Sent, never delivered" fill=#eee
lifeline c "Client"
lifeline s "Server"
fragment f "retry" type=loop class=ghost
operand o "first attempt" in=f class=ghost
message c -> s "request" in=o class=ghost
